---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import WorkHoursCalculator from '../../components/tools/WorkHoursCalculator';
---

<ToolLayout
	title="Work Hours Calculator - Day, week, breaks, overtime estimate | TommyTools"
	description="Free work hours and weekly timesheet calculator: multiple shifts, unpaid breaks, overnight, CSV export, and optional overtime/pay estimates. Runs in your browser."
	heading="Work hours calculator"
	purpose="Build a day or week timesheet from shifts. Subtract unpaid break minutes, handle overnight ends, export CSV or print, and optionally split regular vs overtime hours with a gross pay estimate."
	category="Work hours & shifts"
	categoryHref="/#cat-work-hours"
>
	<div slot="tool">
		<WorkHoursCalculator client:load />
	</div>

	<div slot="instructions">
		<ol>
			<li>Choose <strong>Day</strong> or <strong>Week</strong> mode.</li>
			<li>Enter each shift’s start, end, and unpaid break minutes (0 if none).</li>
			<li>Turn on <strong>Ends next day</strong> when a shift crosses midnight.</li>
			<li>
				Optional: open <strong>Overtime &amp; pay estimate</strong> to set a regular-hour
				threshold, OT multiplier, and hourly rate.
			</li>
			<li>
				Use <strong>Download CSV</strong> or <strong>Print</strong> for a summary that matches
				the on-screen totals.
			</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div slot="example">
		<p>
			<strong>Day:</strong> 09:00–17:30 with a 30-minute unpaid break → net
			<strong> 8 hours</strong> (8.00 decimal).
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Week fixture:</strong> Monday net 8h (with 30m break) plus Tuesday–Friday net 8h
			each, weekend off → <strong>40.00</strong> decimal hours for the week.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Overtime example:</strong> 45 net hours, threshold 40, multiplier 1.5, rate 20 →
			regular 40h / OT 5h; estimated gross pay 950.00 (estimate only).
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="formula">
		<p>
			Elapsed = end − start (+ 24h if ends next day). Net = elapsed − unpaid break. Week total
			sums each day’s net minutes. Overtime hours = max(0, net hours − threshold). Estimated OT
			pay = OT hours × rate × multiplier. Break and OT settings are arithmetic / user-configured -
			not legal classifications. All math runs in your browser.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div slot="limitations">
		<ul>
			<li>Not payroll, tax, or jurisdiction-specific overtime advice.</li>
			<li>Unpaid break is the minutes you enter; the tool does not decide legal deductibility.</li>
			<li>Pay figures ignore taxes, benefits, and deductions.</li>
			<li>
				Week and day workflows share this page (no separate thin SEO clone for “weekly
				timesheet”).
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>


	<div slot="related">
		<ul class="related-list">
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/freelancer-rate">Freelancer rate</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="/tools/advertising-metrics">Advertising metrics</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>

</ToolLayout>
